मूर्ख॑ a. stupid, dull, silly;
 inexperienced in (loc.);
 m.
fool, blockhead.

मूर्छन a. stunning;
 strengthening (—˚). n. increase,
growth;
 f. आ fainting, swooning;
 swelling or rising of sounds,
intonation, note, tone or semitone (in the scale), melody.

मूर्छा f. thickening, coagulation;
 swoon, faint,
stupefaction, astonishment;
 melody.

मूर्छित a. rigid, stiff, thick, strong, intensive, full
of, mixed with (—˚);
 roused, excited;
 stupefied, senseless;
 n. a kind
of song.

मूर्त॑ a. thickened, coagulated, solid, substantial,
corporeal;
 stupefied, insensible.

मू॑र्ति f. (firm) body, embodiment, form, shape, image,
person, adj. —˚ formed of;
 pl. the solid parts of the body.

मूर्धन्य a. being on the head, uppermost, highest,
first;
 cerebral (g.).
